The useOffline configuration option enables offline connectivity detection and automatic retry of failed navigation, prefetch, and Server Action requests. When enabled, it also exposes the useOffline hook for reading the current offline state from Client Components.

import type { NextConfig } from 'next'

const nextConfig: NextConfig = {
  experimental: {
    useOffline: true,
  },
}

export default nextConfig

module.exports = {
  experimental: {
    useOffline: true,
  },
}

When enabled, Next.js will:

Listen for the browser's offline and online events to track connectivity.Detect network failures on navigation, prefetch, and Server Action requests.Poll for connectivity using HEAD requests with backoff while offline.Automatically retry blocked requests once connectivity is restored.Make the useOffline hook available from next/offline.
